- For each `profile_details.documents.<doc>_path`, call `supabase.storage.from_('agent-documents').create_signed_url(path, 3600)` and put the signed URL under `documents.<doc>_url`. Skip docs that have a null path.
- Reuse `_get_trip_counts_by_agent` for `total_trips`.

#### 2.2.2 Extend existing `_serialize_agents`

Add `business_name`, `phone`, `submitted_at` to `AdminManagedAgent` and the serializer — needed so the **list** view (pending tab) can show "Business · CNIC ✓" without an extra round-trip per row.

### 2.3 Frontend — `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`

#### 2.3.1 New private bucket helper

Mirror `uploadProfileImage` but for `agent-documents`. Crucial differences: bucket name, path prefix `agents/<user_id>/`, **does not** call `getPublicUrl` — returns the storage path.

```ts
export async function uploadAgentDocument(
  file: File,
  userId: string,
  kind: "cnic_front" | "cnic_back" | "business_license",
): Promise<string> {
  const ext = file.name.split(".").pop();
  const path = `${userId}/${kind}_${Date.now()}.${ext}`;
  const { data, error } = await supabase.storage
    .from("agent-documents")
    .upload(path, file, { cacheControl: "3600", upsert: true });
  if (error) throw new Error(`Failed to upload ${kind}: ${error.message}`);
  return data.path; // store this in profile_details.documents.<kind>_path
}
```

Note bucket name = `agent-documents`; consider `VITE_SUPABASE_AGENT_DOCS_BUCKET` env override to mirror existing convention.

